        <section id="terminology"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Terminology
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>To understand pure functions, it is helpful to understand some terminology.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Local variable</strong>: when a variable is only held in memory INSIDE a of a function, this is called a LOCAL variable.</li>
<li><strong>Global variable</strong>: a GLOBAL variable is a variable which is held in memory OUTSIDE of a function.</li>
<li><strong>Scope</strong>: this refers to the name of an entity in the code, such as a variable, and where in the code that name can be used. For example a variable would be considered 'out of scope' if it was called and no longer in the memory.</li>
<li><strong>Side effects</strong>: this is when a function changes a variable which is not one of the output variables of the function. For example, changing a global variable from within a function.</li>
</ul>

      </div>
